§ `ss 10(2)-(5), 14; Regulations s 28 -- how much`

-- c060, k044: a standard GP attendance (item 23, Group A1) is prescribed for 100% by reg 28(1).
#ASSERT `Is my service prescribed for 100 per cent` 23 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my service prescribed for 100 per cent` 104 FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is my service prescribed for 100 per cent` 104 TRUE

#ASSERT `What percentage of the Schedule fee is my benefit` `part of an episode of hospital treatment` TRUE EQUALS 75
#ASSERT `What percentage of the Schedule fee is my benefit` `outside any episode of hospital treatment` FALSE EQUALS 85

-- Hypothetical fees. 85% of $39.10 is $33.235, rounded UP to $33.25 (s 10(4)); 85% of $400 is $340, $60 below the fee, so
-- the benefit is $400 - $50 = $350 (s 10(3)); 85% of $333.40 rounds up to $283.40, exactly $50 below, so it stands.
#ASSERT `How much Medicare benefit do I get` 43.90 `outside any episode of hospital treatment` TRUE 43.90 EQUALS 43.9
#ASSERT `How much Medicare benefit do I get` 39.10 `outside any episode of hospital treatment` FALSE 60 EQUALS 33.25
#ASSERT `How much Medicare benefit do I get` 400 `outside any episode of hospital treatment` FALSE 500 EQUALS 350
#ASSERT `How much Medicare benefit do I get` 333.40 `outside any episode of hospital treatment` FALSE 400 EQUALS 283.4
#ASSERT `How much Medicare benefit do I get` 100 `outside any episode of hospital treatment` FALSE 30 EQUALS 30

