§ `ss 10ACA, 10ADA -- the extended Medicare safety net`

#ASSERT `What are my out-of-pocket expenses for the extended safety net` 150 85 EQUALS 65

#ASSERT `Which extended safety-net amount applies to me` printed `a specialist claim well past the general threshold` EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `Which extended safety-net amount applies to me` printed `an FTB(A) family claim past the threshold` EQUALS 500

#ASSERT `Does the extended safety net apply to my claim` printed `a specialist claim well past the general threshold`
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the extended safety net apply to my claim` printed `a specialist claim below the general threshold`)
#ASSERT `Does the extended safety net apply to my claim` printed `a concessional claim crossing the threshold`
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the extended safety net apply to my claim` printed `a claim where less than 20% was paid directly`)

-- The crossing claim: $450 earlier against $500 leaves a balance of $50; 80% x ($100 - $50) = $40 (s 10ADA(8) formula).
-- An FTB(A) family claim of $300 with $350 earlier against $500: balance $150; 80% x ($300 - $150) = $120 (s 10ACA(7)).
#ASSERT `the s 10ADA(8) formula amount` printed `an FTB(A) family claim crossing the threshold` EQUALS 120

#ASSERT `By how much does the extended safety net increase my benefit` printed `a specialist claim well past the general threshold` EQUALS 80
#ASSERT `By how much does the extended safety net increase my benefit` printed `a concessional claim crossing the threshold` EQUALS 40

